## Machine Deck

::bg{location="machine-deck" time="ship-night"}
::vfx{type="frost"}

@purser{code="0010" emotion="level" os}: Coupling five-six is outside tolerance. Release proceeds as scheduled.
@narrator{code="0020"}: The ring had walked a finger's width off its seat. When the shed fired, module five would not let go — it would tear, and take the spine with it.
@toma{code="0030" emotion="frayed" os when="holds(awake(toma))"}: Don't put a hand on that ring. It'll take the arm and thank you for it.
@narrator{code="0040" when="!holds(awake(toma))"}: There was nobody down here to tell you which of the four handles was the one.

/*
  The subject is a dummy. A relation may not be a `<match on>` subject
  (E-MATCH-RELATION-SUBJECT) but IS admitted in a `<when test>`, so the only
  way to gate a BLOCK on `awake(toma)` is to open the match on something the
  guard never reads. See T7 in the drive-test findings log.
*/
<match on="true">
<when test="holds(awake(toma))">
::auto{character="toma" anchor="port" action="brace"}
@toma{code="0050" emotion="clipped"}: Shim's behind you. The steel one. Composite's for people who enjoy fires.
@toma{code="0060" emotion="level"}: Quarter turn. Stop when it stops arguing with you.
::auto{character="toma" action="seal"}
@toma{code="0070" emotion="frayed"}: That's a seat. That's a real seat — it'll let go clean when the time comes.
@toma{code="0080" emotion="hollowed"}: Twelve years I kept this ship's joints honest and it's shedding me a module at a time.
@purser{code="0090" emotion="level" os}: Coupling five-six is within tolerance. Schedule unchanged.
</when>
<otherwise>
@narrator{code="0100"}: You got both hands on the shim, and both hands were not the thing the ring wanted.
::set{run.shedPressure += 1}
::vfx{type="klaxon"}
@purser{code="0110" emotion="level" os}: Coupling five-six remains outside tolerance. Release will be executed with margin. The schedule advances.
@narrator{code="0120"}: Margin. Somewhere in the wall a relay closed on the word, and the ship agreed to lose more than it had planned to.
</otherwise>
</match>

@narrator{code="0130"}: Aft of you a bulkhead picked up the noise and handed it forward, one section at a time, until it reached the part of the ship you were standing in.
